  "provenance": [
    "Native flows use fixed copies of debug smoke builds. Markdown/EPUB passages, PDF passages, and notebook/restart flows were rerun for the control/cancellation corrections. Mixed-size PDF navigation and AT-SPI retain their preceding passing runs. Both full Rust suites and strict Clippy passed; final smoke changes were rebuilt and checked by strict Clippy. The storage permission checks remain applicable and unchanged.",
    "The first reflow run exposed a test setup issue: selecting source text can replace the GTK editor primary selection on X11. The regression compares notebook state immediately before and after capture. All final checks pass.",
    "Earlier September evidence remains historical; this record does not assert those measurements were rerun.",
    "The first timing run passed all application assertions but its restart harness timed out because concurrent Cargo tests replaced the smoke executable with a normal build. All three focused wrappers were rerun successfully using a fixed copy of the smoke binary; these final results include restart checks.",
    "The native controls fixtures use delayed GdkContentProvider delivery and real GtkText/TextBuffer handlers. Source selections and Entry focus can replace the editor primary selection on X11, so each fixture restores its initial editing context. The trusted internal-link fixture uses XTest only on the wrapper-owned private Xvfb display; current-desktop Wayland runs omit that fixture. The first menu-paste fixture was replaced by GTK\u2019s actual Ctrl+V paste action signal because menu action enablement caches clipboard formats until menu/selection activity. All final wrapper and restart checks passed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The Docker host prohibits unprivileged user namespaces. Native tests set WEBKIT_DISABLE_SANDBOX_THIS_IS_DANGEROUS=1 inside this disposable isolated container; these runs do not qualify the WebKit sandbox. No application sandbox setting changed.",
    "AT-SPI assertions are tree/action checks, not a human Orca usability session.",
    "No system installation, actual user-session actions, Wayland scale/performance requalification, or full MVP release qualification was performed. The documented ordinary-reading, human accessibility, and performance gates remain open."
  ],
  "pdf_keyboard_followup": {
    "finding": "SOL-F1: Papers keyboard scroll actions bypassed wheel and selection-changed invalidation.",
    "regression": "Five intended assertions failed before connecting the native scroll action; all 62 PDF passage assertions pass after the fix. The fixture movement check accepts movement within a tall page as well as page-number changes.",
    "assertions_added": 8,
    "behavior": "Keyboard navigation clears the source selection token, Save availability, temporary quotation highlight, and pending passage navigation while programmatic passage restoration keeps its highlight."
  },
  "hosted_review_followup": {
    "documentation": "The original F01/F02 description is explicitly historical, and F02a is marked delivered.",
    "selection": "Focused-chapter deselection and whitespace invalidate capture and temporary marks; delayed deselection from an inactive chapter preserves a newer capture or highlight. Six WebKit adapter assertions cover these cases and the fallback-selection exemption.",
    "pdf_quotation": "Full saved quotations must consist of the ordered per-page fragment text plus whitespace separators. A Rust regression covers Unicode, repeated fragments, normal separators, mismatches, reordering, uncovered text and overlap."
  },
  "hosted_review_timing_followup": {
    "reflow_cancellation": "Recovery snapshots request and selection generations and aborts after document loading and each scan yield. New navigation and appearance commands invalidate selection before queueing. Four WebKit regressions cover navigation, superseding requests, valid replacement requests and delayed document loading.",
    "pdf_page_snapshot": "Paged PDF changes retain the announced page synchronously while deferring coordinates. Stale allocation samples cannot overwrite that page. Four native regressions cover immediate save/bookmark/settings and deferred sampling; 85 mixed-size PDF/navigation assertions also pass."
  },
  "storage_permission_followup": {
    "behavior": "Before SQLite opens on Unix, create or repair the application directory to 0700 and database to 0600. Abort if permission repair fails; do not change existing ancestor permissions.",
    "regressions": "Two Rust regressions run under a separate shell with umask 022 cover fresh creation and repairing 0755/0644 stores while preserving notebook text.",
    "filesystem_checks": {
      "fresh/readero_directory_private": true,
      "fresh/readero_database_private": true,
      "repaired_directory_private": true,
      "repaired_database_private": true,
      "failed_directory_repair_created_no_database": true,
      "failed_database_repair_left_contents_unchanged": true,
      "repaired_store_contents_unchanged": true,
      "new_store_opens": true,
      "repaired_store_opens": true,
      "directory_repair_failure_aborts": true,
      "database_repair_failure_aborts": true,
      "other_uid_cannot_read_notebook_store": true
    },
    "filesystem_probe": "An external core-only probe ran as the container ubuntu user against synthetic fixtures, including non-owned directory/database failures; a different UID was denied reading the private database."
  },
  "navigation_focus_followup": {
    "pdf_context": "Repeated PDF quotations count disjoint UTF-8 spans incrementally rather than recounting each prefix. Two desktop Rust tests cover a 100,002-character dense Unicode page and overlapping Unicode candidates with geometric disambiguation.",
    "pdf_scrollbars": "Both adjustment axes invalidate stale capture tokens, highlights and pending navigation outside programmatic restoration. Sixteen native assertions cover movement, stale capture rejection, clearing/return, restoration, pending requests and fresh selection after scrolling.",
    "notebook_focus": "Compute notebook visibility intent before leaving Focus. Entering Focus flushes the hidden notebook through the existing save/retry path. Five native checks cover both prior visibility states, editor focus, normal toggling afterward and an immediate storage barrier before debounce."
  },
  "control_cancellation_followup": {
    "continuous_scrolling": "Manual scrollbar motion invalidates capture/highlight in Markdown and EPUB. Renderer-owned goTo, chapter insertion/removal, image/font sizing and compensation track their own scroll positions so delayed DOM events preserve verified passage restoration. Native layout checks cover both directions, including manual movement before its scroll event.",
    "paginated_touch": "Touch-style paginator scrollBy/snap movement invalidates old capture and highlighting without treating every shared anchor/layout event as user navigation.",
    "internal_links": "Trusted publication links invalidate pending selection/recovery immediately before queueing navigation. Native XTest activation while the layout queue is held proves immediate invalidation.",
    "relink_dialog": "Cancel, close/Escape and cancelled pending capture leave the quotation and connections intact. The next ordinary capture creates its own reference. Explicit confirmation remains undoable.",
    "capture_intent": "Each capture carries its document generation, operation identity, selection/navigation serial and relink target. Cancellation or a changed target rejects the old reply rather than applying a new intent.",
    "failed_close": "A matching reply retires capture_pending even while close rejects its result. A failed storage close followed by Keep open recovers Save after a fresh selection.",
    "pdf_follow": "Following another saved PDF passage invalidates a previous source capture before programmatic restoration; the new verified highlight remains visible.",
    "shared_reference_history": "Passage names use notebook Undo/Redo through both keyboard handlers and real extra-menu actions inherited by GtkText; rebuilding rows preserves name focus. Native name undo is disabled.",
    "clipboard_sessions": "Changing documents installs a fresh TextBuffer with guarded handlers and transfers notebook marks. Delayed keyboard, menu and primary-selection pastes cannot mutate the new document or retired buffer. Closing/modal states reject deferred edits. GtkEntry guards attach to its actual GtkText delegate and require the currently live widget, preventing late pastes after Undo or row rebuild."
  }
